Because it kicks major butt.  An Archon, to answer someone else's question, is
a form of angel.

The turn after they appear, you get this message:

(assuming you spent one turn (C)alling him "Lothar", as I did)

"Lothar drops a wand.  Lothar drops a polished silver shield. -more-"
"Lothar drops a long sword named Demonbane."

Demonbane is blessed, rustproof, and +1.

This was going to be a great game, I tell you.  Archons also are very powerful
pets--Lothar never took more than three rounds to kill shopkeepers.

I also found a blessed amulet of life saving.

Unfortunately, I also found a level in the Mines with a polymorph trap (or
something)--I was attacked by a titanothere and a balrog without Lothar around
to save me.  Massive stomping.

It's be a nice bones level if I can avoid the balrog, though...

